1. Definitions

“PriveoPDF Code” means the files in this repository in which the rightsholder
owns the relevant rights, excluding third-party components and resources.

“Unmodified Version” means PriveoPDF Code obtained from a revision published by
the rightsholder, without changes other than technical operations strictly
necessary to compile or run it.

“Official Executable” means a binary package published as official by the
rightsholder. It may be accompanied by a separate freeware license.

2. Right to use PriveoPDF

Subject to this license, the rightsholder grants a royalty-free, non-exclusive
right to install and use an Unmodified Version of PriveoPDF for personal use or
the internal professional needs of a person or organization.

This right includes reasonably necessary technical, installation, and backup
copies. It promises no support, maintenance, or availability or free licensing
of any future version.

3. Source review

PriveoPDF Code is made viewable so that its operation can be studied, evaluated,
and audited for security. You may view, download, or clone it and keep private
copies reasonably necessary only for those purposes or for the use permitted by
section 2.

Technical copies and forks provided by the hosting platform are permitted only
to review or audit an Unmodified Version. Copyright notices, this license, and
third-party notices must remain intact.

This is a source-available license. It is not an open-source license.

4. Rights not granted

Unless separately authorized in writing by the rightsholder or allowed by
mandatory law, this license does not permit you to:

- modify PriveoPDF Code or create a derivative work;
- publish or redistribute PriveoPDF Code, a modified version, or a binary
  compiled by a third party beyond the technical copies allowed by section 3;
- sell, rent, sublicense, or transfer PriveoPDF;
- provide PriveoPDF, or a substantially equivalent function, as a service to
  third parties;
- remove or alter ownership, license, or attribution notices; or
- use the PriveoPDF name, marks, or visual assets to imply that a third-party
  version is official.

No contribution, commercial distribution, patent, or trademark right is
granted by implication. All rights not expressly granted are reserved.

5. Third-party components and resources

Third-party components, libraries, fonts, corpora, examples, and other resources
remain governed solely by their own licenses and notices. This license does not
reduce rights granted by those terms, including applicable GNU LGPL rights for
Qt, PySide6, and Shiboken components. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, the licenses/
directory, and the notices supplied with any distribution.

6. Contributions and reports

Repository visibility does not authorize code submissions. External code is
accepted only if the rightsholder publishes separate terms. Factual feedback
and bug reports follow CONTRIBUTING.md. Potential vulnerabilities must follow
SECURITY.md.

7. Termination

The rights granted terminate upon a material breach that remains uncured thirty
days after sufficiently specific written notice. Termination does not affect
rights independently granted by third-party licenses or applicable law.

8. Warranty and liability

PriveoPDF is supplied without an additional voluntary warranty, subject to any
warranties, liabilities, and remedies that applicable law does not allow to be
excluded or limited. To the extent permitted by that law, the rightsholder is
liable only for direct, reasonably foreseeable harm legally attributable to it.
Nothing excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.

9. Mandatory rights and severability

This license does not restrict observation, study, testing, backup,
interoperability, correction, or any other operation that applicable law permits
despite a contractual term. If a term is unenforceable, the remaining terms
continue to the extent permitted.

10. Language

The French text is canonical. This English translation is informative. If they
differ, the French text prevails to the extent allowed by applicable law.
